# The equations of the Reidemeister–Schreier hypotheses

The 46 equations of the authors' code (`Equation1.agda` …
`Equation46.agda`, arXiv ancillary files of 2204.02217), which are the
hypotheses of the Reidemeister–Schreier theorem for the coset data of
`Cosets.lean`: Equations 1–8 are hypothesis (a), one per generator
`ω, H₀, H₁, S₀, S₁, T₀, T₁, CZ`, and Equations 9–46 hypothesis (b),
Equation `9 + 2 (k - 1)` for the coset `I` and relation (Sk) and
Equation `10 + 2 (k - 1)` for the coset `Ω`; they are proved in
`Eqs/Part*.lean`.

Each equation is a packed rewriting certificate checked by
`decide +kernel` on coded words (`QCert.derivable_of_chunks`): both sides
are brought to the same normal form `C · R(P₁) ⋯ R(Pₙ)`, a Clifford
normal form followed by Pauli rotations `R(P) = C_P T₀ C_P⁻¹` (Section 4.3
of the paper) in the lexicographic normal form of their commutation trace,
using the rules of `Cert/Clifford.lean` and `Cert/Rotations.lean`.
Equations 21, 28, 30, 43, 44 and 46 also use the "non-obvious" relations,
at the places where the authors' proofs use them: `lemma-rel-A` (from
(C18)), `lemma-rel-B` (from (C19)) and (C20).  Generated by
`Scratch/CliffordT2/py/gen_equations.py`.
-/
